r: How I learned to start worrying about prompt formatting\nCitations: Sclar2024Formatting\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Preserving Statistical Validity in Adaptive Data Analysis\nCitations: Dwork2015Adaptive\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: The Ladder: A Reliable Leaderboard for Machine Learning Competitions\nCitations: Blum2015Ladder\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Gaussian approximations and multiplier bootstrap for maxima of sums of high-dimensional random vectors\nCitations: Chernozhukov2013Gaussian\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Inference on Winners\nCitations: Andrews2018Winners\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Valid post-selection inference\nCitations: Berk2013PostSelection\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Cross-validation: what does it estimate and how well does it do it?\nCitations: Bates2021CrossValidation\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Interval Estimation for a Binomial Proportion\nCitations: Brown2001Binomial\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Bootstrap Methods: Another Look at the Jackknife\nCitations: Efron1979Bootstrap\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Cross-Validatory Choice and Assessment of Statistical Predictions\nCitations: Stone1974CrossValidation\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: An Introduction to Variable and Feature Selection\nCitations: Guyon2003Selection\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Cross-validation failure: Small sample sizes lead to large error bars\nCitations: Varoquaux2018CrossValidation\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Inference for the Generalization Error\nCitations: Nadeau2003Inference\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Controlling the False Discovery Rate: A Practical and Powerful Approach to Multiple Testing\nCitations: Benjamini1995\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Bias in error estimation when using cross-validation for model selection\nCitations: Varma2006Bias\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Selection bias in gene extraction on the basis of microarray gene-expression data\nCitations: Ambroise2002Selection\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: A survey of cross-validation procedures for model selection\nCitations: Arlot2010Survey\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: On Over-fitting in Model Selection and Subsequent Selection Bias in Performance Evaluation\nCitations: Cawley2010Overfitting\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: No Unbiased Estimator of the Variance of K-Fold Cross-Validation\nCitations: Bengio2004Variance\nLiterature positioning limited to the consulted original abstract or original page: Bootstrap confidence intervals\nCitations: DiCiccio1996Bootstrap\n\nDATA totals: {'attempts': 3, 'correct_programs': 0, 'evaluated_programs': 0, 'ideas': 3}\nFinal status: completed\nFinal outcome: qualified\nFinal metric keys: ['combined_score', 'control_failure_rate', 'correct', 'coverage', 'decision_reversal_rate', 'failure_rate', 'fixed_prompt_mse', 'full_budget_naive_mse', 'honest_half_mse', 'interval_width', 'random_prompt_mse', 'replay_discrepancy', 'report_bias', 'report_mse', 'reuse_mse', 'selected_accuracy', 'signed_optimism']\nTHESIS: Across the five final seeds, half-split reporting lowers mean error relative to reusing the same winner's selection score in the sixteen-prompt conditions, but does not uniformly beat full-budget or non-search comparators, and the real-model results establish audit agreement rather than population validity.\nFRAMING: No previous_paper directory, resolved edit-context file, aggregated directory, or extra_tasks directory is present; this is fresh framing, not a manuscript-preservation decision. The recentered label denotes a move from the task's broad automatic-tuning ambition and private proposal history to the frozen baseline's measured reporting trade-off. There is no prior manuscript title or figure plan to preserve.\n\\subsection{Reproducibility and Resource Accounting}\nThe fixed model revision is \\texttt{12fd25f77366fa6b3b4b768ec3050bf629380bac}; MMLU-Pro is fixed at revision \\texttt{b189ec765aa7ed75c8acfea42df31fdae71f97be}. The retained real pool has $4096$ examples. Normalization uses Unicode NFKC and collapses whitespace; option-content matching sorts normalized options. The split manifest records $11711$ unique groups and allocation seed $732091$. These describe dataset preparation, not additional measured performance. Data may have appeared in pretraining.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/runtime_manifest.json]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/split_manifest.json]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/examples.json]]\n\nThe supplied dependency specification pins NumPy 2.2.6, PyArrow 19.0.1, PyTorch 2.6.0, Transformers 4.51.3, Safetensors 0.5.3, SciPy 1.15.3, and Matplotlib 3.10.3. The runtime manifest identifies CPython 3.12 on Linux x86\\_64, CPU float32 inference and float64 statistics. The answer worker uses two tensor threads and one interoperation thread. These are the supplied environment specification and inspected settings; a separately retained package inventory proving every version actually loaded is unavailable. The paper-artifact environment is recorded separately in the reproduction guide.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/requirements.txt]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/resources/runtime_manifest.json]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L574]]\n\nTo regenerate manuscript analyses without model calls, run \\texttt{python build\\_artifacts.py}. It reads the immutable final record and produces both quantitative figures as PDF and 300-DPI PNG, the main comparison table, the regime table, the complete seed table, and their evidence sidecars. It leaves an orchestrator-rendered overview untouched. The exact final-evaluation entrypoint, resource acquisition details, and validation commands are in \\texttt{REPRODUCIBILITY.md}. Evaluation commands there describe future reproduction, not additional executions during manuscript preparation. Predicted reproduction time is uncertain because the recorded durations include shared caching and orchestration overhead; the measured duration sum is the only supplied wall-time accounting.\n% @evidence[[build_artifacts.py]]\n% @evidence[[analysis/summary.json#/duration_sum_seconds]]\n\nReferences were consulted through fixed original arXiv abstracts, original journal pages, or original publisher-deposited abstracts and bibliographic records, as individually recorded in \\texttt{references\\_provenance.json}. No citation graph or broad topical discovery was used. Full-text reading is not claimed when only an abstract was consulted. No known encounter with the prohibited study occurred. The official ICLR 2026 style and bibliography style were obtained directly from the ICLR template repository, rather than relabeling a template for another year.\n\n\\subsection{LLM Usage}\nLLM-based research assistance contributed to proposal generation, implementation editing, reference planning, narrative selection, plotting code, manuscript drafting, and evidence checking. The research assistance is distinct from the evaluated answer generator, SmolLM2-135M-Instruct. Its role in evaluation is limited to producing the constrained answer letters described in the method. The writing assistant inspected the supplied results and source, generated deterministic summaries and figures, and validated the manuscript; it did not run new scientific inference or simulations for this paper. Literature retrieval used fixed identifiers for permitted originals. No unrecorded human validation, external audit, or independent replication is asserted.\n\n\\end{document}\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n0c8d05ee57b9089de8ab4ab616a6a60a821b2fec4cd787160c668bcc2ded8273  paper.tex\n1c4c7d877fbbfb7cce615c07636d994e1f227a612737598322c9edbabef9392c  references.bib\n6f3cbea8259be1967c7af5bb9b6c8931b177a362b4b90c7598603dc12e7d2423  references_provenance.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
